  <text>
    <body>
      <p>The Sands &amp; McDougall directories list 56 hotels and inns in the project area between 1857 and 1940. Many of them are listed for only a few years. By 1940, the last directory transcribed so far, only 3 were still listed: Carlton Inn (Corkman Hotel), Prince Alfred Hotel and Queensberry Hotel.</p>
      <p>The list below is drawn only from the directories. Each name links to the hotel's own entry, and most of them haven't been written yet. If you know a hotel's story, please start its entry.</p>
      <div>
        <head>Hotels in the directories</head>
        <p>Years are the first and last directories that list the hotel; the directories are yearly to 1880 and then every five years. Corner hotels are often listed under both streets. Street numbers changed when Melbourne's streets were renumbered in the late 1880s, so one hotel can have several numbers.</p>
